# Copy to .env.local. Nothing is required until the stage that introduces it.

# TL-4: the key the unattended agent runs on. Never commit it.
# TL-6: the queue workflow reads it, FACTORY_APP_PRIVATE_KEY (the .pem's contents) and FACTORY_APP_ID
# from the GitHub environment `factory` instead; see platform/queue/README.md.
ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=

# TL-11: run log database. Unset: SQLite in ./.runlog/. TL-12: run-issue.sh writes each run's row here,
# and the queue workflow reads it from the GitHub environment `factory`.
DATABASE_URL=

# TL-6: the factory App's bot login, e.g. my-factory[bot]. run-issue.sh passes its comments (questions, triage
# notes, specs) to the agents; the workflow sets it. Set it for a local review run, which needs the App's spec.
FACTORY_BOT=

# TL-10: the factory's GitHub App, used by `pnpm check-merge-gate` to prove it cannot approve or merge.
FACTORY_APP_ID=
# Path to the App's downloaded .pem private key; keep the file outside the repo.
FACTORY_APP_PRIVATE_KEY_PATH=

# TL-25: Throughline's GitHub App (not the factory's), used by `pnpm check-webhook` to read its webhook
# deliveries and URL. The scheduled workflow reads them from the GitHub environment `throughline`.
THROUGHLINE_APP_ID=
# Path to that App's .pem private key; keep the file outside the repo.
THROUGHLINE_APP_PRIVATE_KEY_PATH=

# TL-3: the private Throughline instance's MCP server, registered in .mcp.json. Claude Code reads
# these from the shell, not from .env.local: export them before starting it.
# The private instance's address (Vercel project throughline-factory, not the public demo), with https:// and no trailing slash.
THROUGHLINE_URL=
# The instance's MCP_TOKEN. Through MCP it can read the roadmap and propose changes, never approve them.
THROUGHLINE_MCP_TOKEN=
# Protection Bypass for Automation secret from the instance's Vercel Deployment Protection settings.
# It opens the whole instance, review queue included, so it can approve proposals outside MCP.
# Export it only for Claude Code sessions you watch, never for unattended runs (scripts/run-issue.sh).
THROUGHLINE_BYPASS_SECRET=
# #35: the MCP gateway's address (platform/mcp-gateway), e.g. https://<gateway-host>, no trailing slash.
# It adds the bypass secret server-side, so a client needs only this and THROUGHLINE_MCP_TOKEN.
THROUGHLINE_GATEWAY_URL=
